  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "Both of you: this case turns on the driver's waiting time at the kerb, and the GPS trace that would show it has a 168-second hole in the middle of that wait. Here is how I have resolved it.\n\nARRIVAL. POL-NS-01 limb (a) and limb (b) are met. The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 12:29:55, and the trace places him inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius before that marker (dwell_start_offset_sec is -5.0), with 35 qualifying in-geofence fixes and a closest approach of 18.1 m at better than the 25 m accuracy filter. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at the marker he was in the radius and stationary, so this was not a false arrival marker, and no POL-NS-05(ii) referral arises. POL-NS-03 is not engaged either: he was inside the 50 m radius, not outside it, and there is a single registered pickup point, so the pin-ambiguity branch is unavailable. POL-NS-04 does not exculpate the rider: the driver replied to her 12:31:02 message at 12:31:20, eighteen seconds later and well inside the 120-second window, so limb (b) of that clause fails.\n\nTHE WAITING PERIOD — THE CRUX. Limb (c) requires the driver to have held position inside the geofence for a CONTINUOUS 300 seconds, measured from his first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the 'arrived' tap. The trace shows two continuous in-geofence runs: 220 seconds (12:30:00–12:33:40) and 112 seconds (12:36:28–12:38:20), separated by a 168-second telemetry gap. The 500-second 'longest_qualifying_run' in the data is not a continuous hold — it is the span from the first to the last fix and it straddles the gap — so it cannot carry limb (c). Nor may the two runs be added: POL-NS-06(i) permits summing only where a present, populated traffic advisory of an admissible type covers the pickup road, and EV-ADVIS-00211-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), so limb (i) is unavailable and the runs stay separate. On the readings that exist, the hold never reaches 300 continuous seconds.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT AN ESCALATION. EV-GPS-00211 is impaired for policy purposes: weight 0.39, issue codes GPS_GAP (168 s, over the 120 s limb in POL-NS-08(b)) and LOW_COVERAGE. Because the gap sits inside the waiting window, whether he stayed put across it is simply not established by the trace, and limb (c) is therefore UNDECIDED over that stretch — not proved and not disproved. The driver's 500-second reading depends on the gap being continuous presence; the rider's 220-second reading depends on the gap being a departure; the trace can certify neither, and a gap in an instrument is not itself evidence that the driver drove off. That alone would be an escalation, because the deciding fact would rest on an impaired artifact alone. It does not, and here is why: the driver's own message at 12:35:10 — 'boss still here waiting ah, cannot see you' — is a contemporaneous record made from inside the unobserved stretch, lying between the in-geofence readings the trace admitted on either side, and the chat log is complete at weight 1.0. Under POL-GEN-02 the deciding fact is accordingly carried by an independent artifact as well, so the cap is the maximum of those carriers and the sole-evidence escalation in POL-NS-08 and POL-NS-09(e) is not engaged. Be clear about what that message does and does not do: it shows he was still working the pickup, not where his car was, so it bridges the gap for confidence purposes but does not prove the hold either. It is a bridge, not a substitute for the test.\n\nTHE OUTCOME. With the continuous dwell undecided, neither the full charge nor a full refund is made out. POL-NS-01 needs limb (c) to hold and it is undecided, so the $4.00 cannot be sustained in full; POL-NS-06 needs the dwell to fall short and it is undecided, so a full refund is not made out either. This is the genuine uncertainty POL-NS-08 provides for, and it directs that the cancellation fee be split rather than allocated whole. The rider is refunded $2.00 of the $4.00 charged; the remaining $2.00 stands. No driver compensation is payable, because POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, which it is not.\n\nCLAIMS ANSWERED. The driver's case that the hold was 500 seconds, and that the weight-1.0 trip record (8.4 minutes) independently proves the hold, is rejected: POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the GPS fixes, not from the 'arrived' event or the arrived-to-cancel span, and the 500-second figure is a span across an unobserved gap. The rider's case that the shortfall is proved is rejected for the mirror-image reason: the 220-second run is read off a trace that is blind for 168 seconds, and the blind stretch is not evidence that the driver left. The rider's POL-NS-04 route is unavailable on the driver's 18-second reply. No escalation trigger in POL-NS-09 fires: there is no unresolved direct contradiction on arrival, dwell or rider presence (POL-NS-01(c) tells us which measure governs), the counterparty-dispute counters are both 0, and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (2 terminations, 1.4% of completed trips), and the non-citable lifetime counters such as prior_no_show_flags play no part in this decision."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.78,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The $4.00 no-show fee is not chargeable; it is refunded to the rider in full and no compensation is payable to the driver.\n\nWhat is not in dispute. EV-TRIP-00211 records the driver's arrival at 12:29:55 and the driver's cancellation at 12:38:20 on reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event, so POL-NS-01(d) is met. The arrival marker is not false: at the marker the driver was inside the 50 m STANDARD radius and stationary (dwell_start_offset_sec -5.0), so POL-NS-05 does not bite. POL-NS-03 is not engaged, because the qualifying fixes are inside the arrival radius and trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, not 2 or more. The driver answered the rider's 12:31:02 message at 12:31:20, eighteen seconds later and with no in-app call, so POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider.\n\nThe case turns on POL-NS-01(c): the driver must have held position inside the pickup geofence for a continuous 300 seconds, measured from the first qualifying GPS fix and not from the arrival tap. EV-GPS-00211 loses 168 seconds from 12:33:40 to 12:36:28, inside the waiting window and over the 120-second trace-defect limb of POL-NS-08(b) - that is the policy-level impairment, in addition to the pre-pass's GPS_GAP and LOW_COVERAGE tags. That artifact carries weight 0.39 and I name it as POL-GEN-02(3) requires. On its admitted readings it shows two separate in-geofence runs: 220 seconds (12:30:00-12:33:40) and 112 seconds (12:36:28-12:38:20). POL-NS-06(i) permits separate in-geofence intervals to be added together only where a present and populated traffic advisory of an admissible type covers the pickup road; EV-ADVIS-00211-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so the runs may not be summed. The 500-second figure the driver relies on is the span from first to last qualifying fix across the gap, not a continuous dwell. The effective dwell is therefore 220 seconds, an 80-second shortfall, and POL-NS-06 refunds the cancellation fee in full with no driver compensation. POL-NS-07 is not reached, so the driver's $3.20 claim fails.\n\nOn the driver's point that the missing 168 seconds are lost telemetry rather than a departure: his own message MSG-00211-004, sent at 12:35:10 from inside the gap, is an independent, unimpaired contemporaneous record (EV-CHAT-00211, weight 1.0). That is why this case is decided rather than escalated - it means the impaired trace is not the only evidence bearing on the disputed window, so POL-NS-08's final sentence and POL-NS-09(e) are not engaged, and the confidence cap is the maximum of the two independent carriers rather than the trace's 0.39. But the message shows the driver was still working the pickup, not that he was inside the arrival radius, and it cannot be substituted for the trace's continuous-presence test. The trip record's wait_time_min of 8.4 is the interval between the two event taps, and limb (c) expressly measures the dwell from GPS, not from the tap; it is in any case the same trip's telemetry rather than an independent carrier of the dwell fact.\n\nEscalation is not required on any other ground: this rider and driver have no prior no-show disputes (0 and 0), the rider's trailing-30-day no-show disputes are 1, and the anti-farming counters (2 terminations over 146 completed trips, 1.4%) do not trip. I have not used the rider's prior_no_show_flags, a lifetime counter, as POL-GEN-01 requires.\n\nRefund: $4.00, being the cancellation-fee line in EV-FARE-00211, which reconciles to the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (both 4.00); no other line was charged on the cancelled trip."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The two in-geofence runs may not be added together. POL-NS-06(i) permits dwell to be accumulated across separate in-geofence intervals only where a traffic_advisory covering the pickup road is PRESENT and POPULATED with an admissible type; EV-ADVIS-00211-01 is MISSING, so limb (i) is unavailable and the 220 second run (12:30:00 to 12:33:40) and the 112 second run (12:36:28 to 12:38:20) stay separate. Without summing, this trace never reaches 300 seconds. I cite the absence of that artifact, which carries weight 0.0, not any content in it; the run figures themselves come from EV-GPS-00211, which I disclose is impaired at weight 0.39 with issue codes GPS_GAP and LOW_COVERAGE.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00211-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Nothing in the chat log makes up the missing seconds. The driver's 12:35:10 message - 'boss still here waiting ah, cannot see you' - was sent from inside the 168 second outage; it shows he was still working the trip, not where his vehicle was, and the chat log's own admissibility note says the same ('it shows he was still working the pickup, though not where he was'). POL-NS-06 is strict liability on the waiting period: the fee is refunded whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she replied, so no message on either side repairs the shortfall.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00211 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "In the alternative, if the Judge declines to find the shortfall on this trace, the disputed $4.00 still cannot be left collected. The effective dwell is carried by a single artifact, EV-GPS-00211, whose weight_multiplier is 0.39 and which is impaired under POL-NS-08(b) because its 168 second gap exceeds the 120 second threshold. Under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence in any ruling resting on that artifact is capped at 0.39, below the 0.70 platform floor, and POL-NS-09(a) and POL-NS-09(e) therefore require the case to go to a human reviewer with the fee held rather than collected or refunded. A held fee is not a rider loss; NO_ACTION, which would leave the $4.00 charged and refund_issued_sgd at 0.00, is.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00211 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The 0.39 weight on the trace should not be read as capping this ruling below the 0.70 floor. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the cap is the minimum weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding fact, except that where two or more independent artifacts carry it the cap is the maximum of their multipliers. The continuous-hold fact is carried by the trace and, independently, by the weight-1.0 trip record (arrival 12:29:55, cancellation 12:38:20, wait_time_min 8.4) and by the weight-1.0 chat log (the driver's message at 12:35:10 from inside the outage). The deciding fact is therefore not carried solely by the impaired trace, and the final-sentence escalation route in POL-NS-08 is not engaged.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-GPS-00211 at weight_multiplier 0.39 but does not name its issue code(s): GPS_GAP, LOW_COVERAGE"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The driver does not need, and does not rely on, POL-NS-06(i). That limb exists to let separate in-geofence intervals be added together, and it requires a present and populated traffic_advisory of type KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT. EV-ADVIS-00211-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 - no advisory covers Toa Payoh Central in this window - and its absence is neutral here: the driver's case is a single continuing presence, so there are no separate intervals to sum and nothing turns on the missing advisory.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00211-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "Both sides' cases turn on one question: did the driver hold the pickup for the STANDARD minimum of 300 seconds before cancelling?\n\nTo the rider: your claim is not supported and the $4.00 cancellation fee stands. Every route you raised fails on the record. POL-NS-04 (driver failed to answer) fails at limb (b) - you wrote 'coming down now, 2 min' at 12:31:02 and the driver replied 'ok waiting outside 79' at 12:31:20, eighteen seconds later, so the clause does not apply whatever the reply said. POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) does not bite: at the 12:29:55 marker the driver was already inside the 50 m STANDARD radius and stationary, so there is no false marker and no false-arrival referral. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) is not engaged: he was inside the arrival radius, and only one pickup point is registered. That leaves the waiting-period shortfall, and it does not run. The GPS trace is impaired - weight 0.39, issue codes GPS_GAP and LOW_COVERAGE - because a 168-second sampling gap (12:33:40 to 12:36:28) exceeds the 120-second limb in POL-NS-08(b) and splits the trace into a 220-second and a 112-second run. But a gap is missing telemetry, not a recorded departure, and it is bridged by unimpaired evidence: the driver's message at 12:35:10, sent and delivered from inside the gap ('boss still here waiting ah, cannot see you'), read at 12:35:26, and the identical kerbside position either side of it (18.1 m from the pin; 0.0 km straight-line between the bracketing fixes). A contemporaneous record made from inside the unobserved stretch, lying between readings the trace did admit, is evidence of what was happening then even though it does not itself fix a coordinate. The hold therefore runs continuously from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 12:30:00 to the 12:38:20 cancellation - over 300 seconds. The 220-second run and the 80-second 'shortfall' appear only if the gap is read as a departure, which nothing establishes; POL-NS-06(i) is not needed, because this is one continuing attempt, not two intervals to be summed. Your own messages (12:31:02, and 'i was at the door already' at 12:38:45) are consistent with a late arrival, and your rider track being near the pin is immaterial to the arithmetic.\n\nTo the driver: POL-NS-01 is satisfied on all four limbs - a recorded 'arrived' event at 12:29:55; qualifying in-geofence fixes before it (35 fixes, closest 18.1 m, at 6.1 to 11.9 m accuracy, inside the 25 m filter); an unbroken hold beyond the 300-second STANDARD minimum; and no boarding event with a driver termination at 12:38:20 on RIDER_NO_SHOW. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so you are compensated under POL-NS-07 at 80 percent of the $4.00 fee - SGD 3.20. The anti-farming check does not withhold it: no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2 of 146 completed trips is 1.4 percent (below 8 percent). The fee itself is not refunded; the $3.20 is a platform-funded payment to you, and amount_sgd carries the same figure under POL-GEN-03.\n\nOn weight: the continuous hold is carried by the impaired GPS trace (0.39) and independently by the chat log (weight 1.0), a contemporaneous record from inside the gap, so under POL-GEN-02(2) the cap is the maximum of the independent carriers' weights - 1.0 - and confidence is 0.85, above the 0.70 escalation floor. No escalation trigger fires and no clause produces a referral; the only residual open point, whether the driver moved during the 168 seconds the trace does not cover, is answered as far as the record allows by the bridged account above."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
